WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
- Well, you've been open
about identifying as queer.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.737
- Yes.

00:00:02.737 --> 00:00:03.990
- So, were you able to
embrace that as a teenager?

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:04.823
Was that easy?

00:00:04.823 --> 00:00:06.637
- No, because I don't
think I had the language.

00:00:06.637 --> 00:00:07.470
- Oh.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.330
- To even know what was going on.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.230
I think it's come much later to me, now.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.670
And it's wonderful

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.550
to just be me.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.050
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Really, yeah.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:19.883
- Refreshing.

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:20.880
- Yes, very much so.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.820
And I think it sort of
made space, creatively,

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.690
to just sort of let go
of whatever I was hiding.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.300
I guess, you know, you don't
realize you're doing that,

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.070
putting so much energy behind it.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.690
And once you take the energy away

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.800
from concealing something
that is so a part of you,

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.800
that you can't hide it,
you can put it elsewhere.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:43.703
- Absolutely.

00:00:43.703 --> 00:00:45.270
- Make more wonderful things.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.280
- When you say like, you
didn't know the language.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.350
You mean like, there just
wasn't a lot around you

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.760
that kind of, even, you didn't even,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:51.990
you knew it was happening,

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.670
but you didn't know what to say about it?

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:54.630
- What's to say about, yeah.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.820
I knew something was different.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.290
Particularly when I talk about that,

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:02.010
I knew something was different
but I didn't know what.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.110
Like, how, what do I call it?

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.790
What do I say about it, now?

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.170
- I've never heard someone
describe it like that.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.550
And that's so poignant.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.550
- Yeah, I think sometimes we
assume that every queer person

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.083
knows it from the beginning.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.460
Most of us do, but we don't
necessarily know the language.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.110
Until someone says, hey, this is,

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.570
these are words that
you might want to use.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.120
These are expressions that
you might want to use.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:27.953
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:29.983
- This is, here is some space for you.

00:01:29.983 --> 00:01:30.816
- Yeah.

00:01:30.816 --> 00:01:32.100
- So you can speak about yourself

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.220
without someone else telling you.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.350
- And I think finding your
people, like, when you're young,

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.020
like, your people to kind of help you.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:39.853
- [Cynthia] Yeah.

00:01:39.853 --> 00:01:41.010
- Like, cultivate, and
all of us, you know,

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.510
our personalities, our
character, like who we are.

